DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzmmoonn is the system monitor of the COHERENT GUI.  It must be
     run under the zzvviieeww desktop.  Every 3 seconds it takes a
     snapshot of the kernel through /ddeevv/kkmmeemm and redraws what
     changed: a memory total line, a bar of user memory in use, a
     breakdown grid (kernel, arena, buffers, segments, stacks,
     system, shared, saving, free, holes, largest), and a process
     list in ppss style - PID, user, size, tty, state, time and
     command.  The display is read-only; there is no way to sig-
     nal or kill a process from it.  zzmmoonn accepts the standard
     window _o_p_t_i_o_n_s of GUI applications; see zzvviieeww.

     The only keys scroll the process list:

                ^PP, ^NN          up / down one line
                ^ZZ, ^BB          up one page
                ^VV, ^FF, SSPPAACCEE   down one page

     The state column shows RR running, SS sleeping, WW waiting, TT
     stopped and ZZ defunct.  Command lines that cannot be read
     show as <ddeeffuunncctt>, <iiddllee>, <sswwaapp> or <sslliibb>.

FFIILLEESS
                  /coherent             kernel image, for the symbol table
                  /dev/kmem             kernel memory (required)
                  /dev/mem, /dev/swap   command lines (optional)

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     zzvviieeww, ppss

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     When the kernel cannot be read, the memory pane shows
     `Memory: no data' with the reason beneath: `(bad namelist in
     /coherent)', `(cannot open /dev/kmem)', `(kernel memory read
     error)', `(out of memory)'.

NNOOTTEESS
     Reading /ddeevv/kkmmeemm requires the usual permission; without it
     zzmmoonn runs but shows no data.  Without /ddeevv/mmeemm only the com-
     mand column degrades.  At most 96 processes are shown.  The
     refresh interval is fixed.
